# Wave W17-N (Route 112): gondola post base — a cable-car post BASE on the chimney road: a heavy timber footing block with the post’s iron-banded stub standing in it, built to carry the design’s wires (the wires themselves are design dressing — no shipped wire kind, nothing strung). On fume turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the route marker posts by its footing block and iron band: this is a foundation, not a signpost.
